        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: recover interrupted command dispatches",
        "body": "## What changed\n\nThis keeps the useful pre-dispatch claim from #380, but makes the claim recoverable instead of terminal.\n\n- Every review, assist, and repair dispatch now carries a deterministic receipt key.\n- A retry first looks for the exact Actions run created after the durable claim. Active runs keep the claim waiting, successful runs finalize recovery, and cancelled, failed, skipped, or timed-out runs become retryable after the visibility window.\n- The receiving queue and workflows deterministically give the oldest active or successful same-key run ownership, while later duplicates and failed older runs cannot suppress all execution.\n- The review path no longer falls back to an untraceable second dispatch mechanism.\n- Active repair detection recognizes keyed run names, including issue-implementation titles, and the waiting claim keeps its original timestamp.\n- Synthetic label-sweep commands recover prior claims by stable idempotency key even though their per-run timestamps change.\n\nThis replacement was necessary because the contributor branch allows maintainer edits but the available personal OAuth authorization cannot update workflow files. The final tree preserves and extends @ag-linden's work, with co-author credit in both commits.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Crash/retry runtime smoke: `crash_before_dispatch=wait`, `crash_after_dispatch=recover`, `stale_without_receipt=dispatch`.\n- Focused router/workflow/capacity tests: 184 passed.\n- Full repository proof: 600 unit tests and 612 repair tests passed; both instrumented coverage modes passed after removing a 10-second test-only scheduler race.\n- Changed coverage: 100% lines, 89.17% branches, 100% functions.\n- Overall coverage: 76.67% lines, 70.66% branches, 83.97% functions.\n- Build, lint, formatting, active-surface, workflow-input, and automation-limit checks passed.\n- AutoReview: no accepted or actionable findings; patch correct at 0.84 confidence.\n\n## Risk\n\nMedium. This changes command-dispatch recovery and three receiving workflows. API-read failures fail closed, claims wait five minutes before stale recovery, failed receipts remain retryable, and receiver-side ownership prevents duplicate execution without losing all copies.\n\nReplaces #380.\n",
